    "focal_pair": {
      "annotated_sentence_text": "[Turn 7 USER]\ne059\tI am leaning toward accepting a four-month, twice-monthly program at Willow Hub, but only if we recruit one named site coordinator and finish the first version of the drop-in curriculum before launch.\ne060\tI want to tell participants from the beginning that the schedule will be reviewed after four months.\ne061\tMy volunteer lead thinks those conditions are reasonable, although she worries the curriculum requirement will become another delay.\ne062\tI have not decided what happens if we find the coordinator but the materials are only partly ready.\n[Turn 7 ASSISTANT]\ne063\tThat is a conditional direction, not a disguised final answer, and the unresolved point matters.\ne064\tYou could define what “ready enough” means in terms of what a participant and volunteer must be able to do, rather than whether every planned material is finished.\ne065\tBut setting that threshold will still involve judgment, and your colleague may reasonably challenge it.\ne066\tThe most useful next conversation is probably not “are we expanding?”\ne067\tbut “which imperfections are we willing to carry into a time-limited public commitment, and who carries them?”",
